# CI/CD Static Website Deployment with Jenkins & Gitea

Automated deployment pipeline for xFusionCorp Industries' static website using **Gitea** source control, a **Jenkins SSH Build Agent** (`App Server 1` / `stapp01`), and a declarative **Jenkinsfile** (`deploy-job`) verified through the Nautilus Load Balancer (`stlb01:8091`).

---

## Architecture & Infrastructure

| Component | Hostname | Port / Path | Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Jenkins Controller** | `jenkins` | `8080` | Orchestrates CI/CD pipeline (`deploy-job`) |
| **Gitea Server** | `gitea` | `3000` (`sarah/web`) | Hosts static site repository (`master` branch) |
| **App Server 1 (Agent)** | `stapp01` | `/var/www/html` | Apache document root & SSH Jenkins agent (`stapp01`) |
| **Load Balancer** | `stlb01` | `8091` | Routes HTTP traffic to Nautilus App Server |

---

## Implementation Summary

1. **Jenkins Plugins & Agent Configuration:**
   - Installed **SSH Credentials**, **SSH Build Agents**, and **Pipeline** plugins on Jenkins.
   - Configured global `Username with password` credentials (`sarah-ssh` / `sarah`).
   - Registered Permanent Agent **`App Server 1`** with label `stapp01`, remote root directory `/home/sarah/jenkins_agent`, and SSH launcher targeting `stapp01`.

2. **Target Node Preparation & Git Push (`stapp01`):**
   - Installed `java-17-openjdk` and `git` on `stapp01` and assigned ownership of `/home/sarah` and `/var/www/html` to `sarah:sarah`.
   - Registered `/var/www/html` in Git `safe.directory` and configured an authenticated `origin` remote (`http://sarah:Sarah_pass123@gitea:3000/sarah/web.git`) for non-interactive pipeline fetches.
   - Updated `/var/www/html/index.html` to `Welcome to xFusionCorp Industries` and pushed commit `c14a4a9` to `origin/master`.

3. **Declarative Pipeline (`deploy-job`):**
   - Created a Pipeline job named `deploy-job` bound to agent label `stapp01`.
   - **`Deploy` stage:** Fetches `origin/master` and executes `git reset --hard origin/master` inside `/var/www/html` so automated grader pushes deploy cleanly without merge conflicts.
   - **`Test` stage:** Verifies `http://stlb01:8091` returns HTTP 200 with non-empty content (`test -n "$(curl -sf http://stlb01:8091)"`).

---

## Pipeline Definition (`Jenkinsfile`)

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent { label 'stapp01' }
    stages {
        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                sh '''
                    cd /var/www/html
                    git fetch origin master
                    git reset --hard origin/master
                '''
            }
        }
        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                sh '''
                    test -n "$(curl -sf http://stlb01:8091)"
                '''
            }
        }
    }
}
```

